&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soho, London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid working: 3 days in the office Tues - Thurs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To provide technical leadership and hands-on contribution within a data engineering team, designing, building, and optimizing robust data pipelines and infrastructure for a global sports betting and media business. This role is crucial in delivering high-quality data solutions that support LiveScore’s strategic goals and embody our commitment to being Fan Driven and a Champion of Sport. You will mentor junior engineers and ensure technical excellence in your domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At LiveScore Group, we’re the proud home of three of the most exciting brands in the sports and gaming world: LiveScore, LiveScore Bet and Virgin Bet. A fully owned and operated ecosystem that converges the two worlds of sports media and sports betting. We’re proud of the high ratings for our commitment to excellence and fueling fan’s passion for sport driving us to the top.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don’t just lead; we innovate. Our cutting-edge products and immersive experiences set the standard, but it’s our people who truly make the difference. Every day, our team embody our values: adaptability, teamwork, a fan-driven approach, and an ever-curious mindset that fuels our ambition. As we scale and continue to create a culture that allows all employees to thrive, we know we need the most talented people with diverse backgrounds, perspectives and skills. If you’re good at what you do, come and join us. The more inclusive we are, the more amazing experiences we can create for our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We know that job descriptions can sometimes seem daunting, and you might not feel you tick every box. But, if you’re passionate about the role and have relevant experience, we want to hear from you!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership and Guidance:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a primary technical point of contact and subject matter expert for specific data engineering projects or domains, guiding team members through complex technical challenges and promoting innovative solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Data Solution Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, develop, test, and deploy highly scalable, reliable, and fault-tolerant data pipelines and ETL/ELT processes. This includes data ingestion from diverse sources, data transformation, and data loading into various data stores (e.g., data warehouses, data lakes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architectural Implementation:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Data Architects to translate architectural blueprints and standards into concrete implementations, ensuring new data components align with the overall data strategy and infrastructure requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentorship and Skill Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively mentor and coach junior and mid-level data engineers, providing constructive feedback, sharing technical knowledge, and fostering their growth in coding, data modeling, and general data engineering best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-On Contribution:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain a significant hands-on role in coding, data modeling, infrastructure-as-code development, and platform configuration, leading by example and ensuring high-quality output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Quality and Performance Assurance:&lt;/strong&gt; Take direct responsibility for ensuring the quality, integrity, and performance of data assets within their assigned domain or projects, implementing monitoring, validation, and optimization strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Efficiency and Cost Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively identify and implement technical optimizations for data processing, storage, and infrastructure utilization to improve efficiency, reduce operational costs, and enhance system performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code Review and Best Practices:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead and participate in rigorous code reviews, advocating for and enforcing engineering best practices, coding standards, and architectural patterns to maintain high code quality and system stability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complex Problem Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Diagnose, troubleshoot, and provide effective solutions for highly complex data-related issues, incidents, and performance bottlenecks, often working under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate effectively with other engineering teams, product managers, data scientists, and business stakeholders to understand data requirements, integrate solutions, and provide technical insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills, Knowledge and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced Data Pipeline Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven, in-depth experience as a senior or lead data engineer with a strong portfolio of hands-on contributions to designing, building, and optimizing complex, large-scale data pipelines and ETL/ELT processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Data Warehousing (EDW) and Data Modeling:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong practical experience with EDW concepts, principles, and implementation, specifically including the design and practical application of a single, integrated data model for analytical purposes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud Data Platforms:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with cloud-native data services and infrastructure on at least one major cloud provider (e.g., AWS services like S3, Redshift, Glue, EMR; GCP services like BigQuery, Dataflow, Pub/Sub; Azure services like Data Lake, Synapse Analytics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cost Optimization Strategies:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to identify, propose, and implement technical solutions that lead to significant cost savings in data processing, storage, and infrastructure within a large-scale data environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Engineering Fundamentals:&lt;/strong&gt; Expert proficiency in software development methodologies (e.g., Agile, Scrum), version control (Git), CI/CD pipelines, automated testing, and comprehensive understanding of software engineering best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional coding skills in at least one relevant programming language (e.g., Python, Scala, Java, JavaScript, C/C++), with a focus on writing clean, efficient, and maintainable code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Database Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Extensive experience with various database technologies including relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL), NoSQL databases (e.g., MongoDB, Cassandra), and analytical data warehouses (e.g., Snowflake, Redshift, BigQuery).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Architecture Principles:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid understanding of data architecture patterns (e.g., Data Mesh, Data Lakehouse, Lambda/Kappa architectures), distributed systems, and their practical application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience in developing and maintaining robust and auditable data solutions for regulatory reporting, particularly within the gaming or other highly regulated industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluent in AI prompting alongside staying ahead of emerging AI technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership &amp;amp; Mentorship:&lt;/strong&gt; A natural leader who can effectively guide, inspire, and technically mentor junior and mid-level engineers. Possesses the ability to break down complex problems, provide clear direction, and foster a learning environment, thereby enhancing team capabilities and promoting adherence to best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What can we offer?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Performance Bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Working Agreements where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Healthcare Scheme + Employee Enhanced Assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced Family Leave - Maternity, Shared Parental &amp;amp; Adoption Leave: up to 6 months at full pay and 6 months at half pay. Paternity leave: up to 4 weeks at full pay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidised Gym Membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual Travel Card Loan &amp;amp; Ride to Work Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance (x3 salary)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributory Pension Plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Virgin Family: Giving you access to exclusive Virgin offers and experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thursday drinks in the office and regular socials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ReqID:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; FEQ427R149&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills: Networking, Security, Platform, DevOps, Databricks, Cloud - AWS, GCP, Azure, Infrastructure - First preference would be GCP experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruiter: Dina Hussain&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Infrastructure &amp;amp; Platform Specialist Solutions Engineer, you will serve as a trusted technical advisor, helping enterprise customers with the architecture, administration, and security of their Databricks deployments on their cloud of choice (AWS, Azure, or GCP). You combine solid technical expertise with a growing ability to connect architecture decisions to customer outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Impact You Will Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide enterprise customers through the full lifecycle of Databricks on their cloud platform, including platform administration from initial architectural design to production deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect secure, scalable enterprise deployments that satisfy complex cloud networking (virtual networks, private connectivity), identity (cloud IAM and enterprise identity providers), and security compliance standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a technical specialist in core areas such as cloud infrastructure, infrastructure-as-code (IaC), cloud networking, and identity management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support technical wins in competitive scenarios by demonstrating Databricks&#39; differentiation through custom-built solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional resources (DSAs, SAs, FDE, Partners) to contribute to solutions for complex customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with growing autonomy on well-scoped engagements, with guidance from senior architects on the most complex designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence product direction by providing structured feedback on customer requirements and competitive gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We Look For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years in solutions architecture, technical pre-sales, or a Network architecture hands-on technical role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise across the following areas:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security &amp;amp; Identity:&lt;/strong&gt; Cloud security controls, platform/network/data security, encryption, vulnerability management, compliance, and identity protocols. This includes cloud-native IAM (AWS IAM, Microsoft Entra ID / Azure AD, Google Cloud IAM), enterprise identity services (AWS IAM Identity Center, Entra ID, Google Cloud Identity), and federation standards (SCIM, OAuth, SAML, OIDC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Networking &amp;amp; Deployments:&lt;/strong&gt; Enterprise cloud networking (VPC/VNet design and peering, dedicated interconnects such as AWS Direct Connect / Azure ExpressRoute / Google Cloud Interconnect, and private connectivity such as AWS PrivateLink / Azure Private Link / GCP Private Service Connect), network routing, performance optimisation, and large-scale deployment management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Administration:&lt;/strong&gt; High availability, disaster recovery, cluster orchestration, observability and audit (e.g. Amazon CloudWatch / CloudTrail, Azure Monitor, Google Cloud Operations Suite), and cloud cost management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure Automation (InfraOps):&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on automation using IaC tools (e.g. Terraform, plus cloud-native tooling such as AWS CloudFormation / CDK, Azure Resource Manager / Bicep, or Google Cloud Deployment Manager) to build, maintain, and scale complex cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding proficiency in Python and PySpark/Spark: you must demonstrate live coding, debugging, and solution-building skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid grounding in distributed data systems architecture: scalable pipelines, streaming architectures, lakehouse patterns, and cloud-native data platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient on the Databricks Platform (or demonstrated ability to achieve proficiency rapidly) with a developing technical specialisation in one area (e.g. real-time/streaming, ML/AI, data governance, migrations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to contribute to architecture discussions with senior technical stakeholders: whiteboarding, design reviews, and trade-off analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of driving platform adoption and consumption growth within accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Field Engineering thought leadership through customer-facing content, workshops, and community engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills: able to translate complex architectures into business value for both technical and executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a quantitative discipline (or equivalent experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 30% as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Databricks certifications (Data Engineer, ML, Platform)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud provider certifications at professional level (e.g. AWS Certified Solutions Architect – Professional or AWS Certified Data Engineer; Azure Solutions Architect Expert; Google Professional Cloud Architect)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with competitive platforms (Snowflake, cloud-native data services, Azure Synapse, BigQuery), understanding the landscape you&#39;ll position against&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in a data/AI company or cloud provider&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
